# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PILOT CORPUS — james-habits-app
#
# James, #68 (2026-08-30): "Let's pilot it on the non technical apps for now:
# habits app, vocab app."
#
# Nothing here is invented. Every DEFINED behaviour traces to a line in
# james-habits-app's own docs/DESIGN.md or to his issue #1. Every INFERRED
# behaviour traces to a named test method or route registration that exists on
# origin/dev at e75de89. The `source` line on each behaviour is the trace, and
# it is checkable — the whole point is that a reader can go and look.
#
# Per his decision on #68 (2026-08-30): inferences are INCLUDED BY DEFAULT but
# carry `review unreviewed` until he adjudicates them. They are not silently
# folded into the spec.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═══ DEFINED — the product as docs/DESIGN.md states it ═══
#
# These are the behaviours a human wrote down. Note what happens to them below:
# the frontend on origin/dev is still the untouched web-template scaffold (one
# Home page), so every noun these name is missing from the app. The generator
# refuses them and says which noun is absent. That refusal is the measurement of
# "defined but not built" — nobody had to maintain a list.

behaviour BEH-TODAY-1 "The day's habits are listed in order so the whole day can be logged from one screen"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-3
  actor owner
  when opens page:Today
  then sees region:HabitList
  then sees control:DateStepper

behaviour BEH-TODAY-2 "A checkbox habit is ticked inline"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-3
  actor owner
  given habit:BooleanSeeded
  when opens page:Today
  when activates checkbox:HabitRow
  then sees badge:Streak

behaviour BEH-TODAY-3 "A numeric habit takes a value in a number field"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-3
  actor owner
  given habit:NumericSeeded
  when opens page:Today
  when fills field:HabitValue with ?value
  then sees badge:Streak

behaviour BEH-TODAY-4 "Previous days can be reached with the date stepper and back-filled"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A2
  actor owner
  when opens page:Today
  when activates control:DateStepperBack
  then sees region:HabitList

behaviour BEH-MANAGE-1 "Habits can be added, renamed, reordered and archived"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-4
  actor owner
  when opens page:Manage
  then sees button:AddHabit
  then sees region:HabitEditor

behaviour BEH-HISTORY-1 "Each habit shows a 30-day completion grid with current and longest streak"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-5
  actor owner
  when opens page:History
  then sees region:CompletionGrid
  then sees badge:CurrentStreak
  then sees badge:LongestStreak

# The design's hard constraint. It is deliberately a `contract`: a behaviour tree
# has no honest way to assert a wall-clock budget over a human, and hiding it
# would flatter the coverage number by deleting the requirement most likely to be
# missed. Something else must own this — today, nothing does.
behaviour BEH-LOOP-1 "The full day is loggable from one screen in under ~20 seconds"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#product-shape
  actor owner
  contract the whole day is loggable from one screen in under ~20 seconds

# A7 is an assumption with a real failure mode (timezones) and no test anywhere
# in the repo names it. Recorded so that absence is visible rather than implied.
behaviour BEH-DATE-1 "The client's local calendar day is stored verbatim as YYYY-MM-DD"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A7
  actor owner
  contract the server stores the client-supplied YYYY-MM-DD date without timezone conversion


# ═══ INFERRED — what the code actually asserts today ═══
#
# Read out of the 41 backend test method names and the route registrations.
# Every one is `review unreviewed` per his #68 decision. Several of these are
# behaviours no document states — that is the "built but never specified" half,
# and it is the half a spec-first tool normally cannot see at all.

behaviour BEH-SEED-1 "First run is not empty — a starter set of habits is seeded exactly once"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.Habits.Tests/HabitServiceTests.cs:EnsureSeeded_creates_the_starter_set_once
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-TODAY-1
  actor owner
  when opens page:Today
  then sees region:HabitList
  contract seeding is idempotent — a second run does not duplicate the starter set

behaviour BEH-ORDER-1 "A newly created habit is appended to the end of the display order"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.Habits.Tests/HabitServiceTests.cs:Create_appends_to_the_end_of_the_order
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-TODAY-1
  actor owner
  contract POST /api/habits places the new habit last in sortOrder

behaviour BEH-ARCHIVE-1 "An archived habit disappears from the list but stays retrievable by id"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.Habits.Tests/HabitApiTests.cs:Archive_hides_the_habit_but_keeps_it_retrievable
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-MANAGE-1
  actor owner
  contract DELETE /api/habits/{id} archives rather than deletes
  contract GET /api/habits omits the archived habit
  contract GET /api/habits/{id} still returns it

# NO `serves` LINE, ON PURPOSE — and this is the whole point of his frontend-first
# answer. MVP 4 is "add/edit/archive habits"; nothing in DESIGN.md describes a
# screen that ever SHOWS an archived habit. So `?includeArchived=true` exists to
# satisfy no display. Either the Manage screen needs an "archived" view that the
# design forgot to state, or the flag should go. Kit will not pick.
behaviour BEH-ARCHIVE-2 "Archived habits can be asked for explicitly"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.Habits.Tests/HabitServiceTests.cs:GetAll_excludes_archived_unless_asked
  review unreviewed
  actor owner
  contract GET /api/habits takes a flag that includes archived habits
  asks "Should the Manage screen gain a view of archived habits, or should the includeArchived flag go?"
  option "Add the view" "DESIGN.md MVP 4 gains an archived view. The flag earns a documented reason to exist and the frontend gets something to build. More surface on an app whose screens are not built yet."
  option "Delete the flag" "GetAll stops taking it and one backend test goes with it. Archived habits stay retrievable by id (BEH-ARCHIVE-1), so nothing is lost — but un-archiving through the UI becomes a new decision if you ever want it."
  recommend "Add the view" "Archiving is already a one-way door in the UI: DELETE archives rather than deletes, so a habit archived by mistake is reachable from no documented screen. The flag is not spare surface — it is the missing half of a capability MVP 4 already promises."
  against "MVP 4 promises archiving, not un-archiving, and none of the three screens exists yet — this adds scope to an app whose Today screen is not built. Deleting the flag costs one test, and the day you want the view you write it then against a design that states it. Keeping unused surface because it might be needed is exactly how an API grows features nobody asked for."

behaviour BEH-STREAK-1 "Today counts as a grace day — an unlogged today does not break the streak"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.Habits.Tests/HabitCalculatorTests.cs:CurrentStreak_treats_today_as_a_grace_day_when_not_yet_done
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-TODAY-2
  serves BEH-HISTORY-1
  actor owner
  given habit:BooleanSeeded
  when opens page:Today
  then sees badge:Streak
  contract the streak counts back from today and tolerates today being unlogged

behaviour BEH-STREAK-2 "A streak stops at the first missed day"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.Habits.Tests/HabitCalculatorTests.cs:CurrentStreak_stops_at_the_first_gap
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-HISTORY-1
  actor owner
